{"key":"enterprise/T1195.003","id":"T1195.003","name":"Compromise Hardware Supply Chain","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1195","tactics":["initial-access"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may manipulate hardware components in products prior to receipt by a final consumer for the purpose of data or system compromise. By modifying hardware or firmware in the supply chain, adversaries can insert a backdoor into consumer networks that may be difficult to detect and give the adversary a high degree of control over the system. Hardware backdoors may be inserted into various devices, such as servers, workstations, network…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1195/003","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--39131305-9282-45e4-ac3b-591d2d4fc3ef","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:39.693Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0079","name":"Driver Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0079","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3551476e-14f5-4e48-a518-e82135329e03","page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0018","name":"Host Status","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0018","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--85a533a4-5fa4-4dba-b45d-f0717bedd6e6","page":"telemetry/DC0018/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0368","name":"Hardware Supply Chain Compromise Detection via Host Status & Boot Integrity Checks","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--4dfcf95f-0bbb-4ae7-8bd5-91e3e6c51809","relationship_id":"relationship--37fa991d-a766-4131-9843-441d5bbe763b"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1035","name":"Analytic 1035","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1035","guidance":"Detects tampered hardware or firmware via anomalous host status telemetry. Behavioral chain: (1) Pre-OS or firmware components exhibit unexpected version changes, signature failures, or modified boot paths; (2) System management/firmware tools log hardware inventory drift; (3) Sensor health telemetry or boot attestation events fail baseline checks; (4) Follow-on process execution from altered firmware or unknown drivers after boot.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0368"},{"id":"AN1036","name":"Analytic 1036","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1036","guidance":"Monitors for hardware or firmware tampering by correlating system boot logs, hardware inventory changes, and secure boot/firmware verification failures. Behavioral chain: (1) UEFI/BIOS version drift; (2) secure boot disabled or signature verification errors; (3) unexpected modules or hardware devices enumerated at boot; (4) new device firmware images loaded from non-approved sources.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0368"},{"id":"AN1037","name":"Analytic 1037","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1037","guidance":"Detects tampered Mac hardware/firmware by analyzing unified logs, EndpointSecurity events, and Apple Mobile File Integrity (AMFI) checks. Behavioral chain: (1) Boot process reports firmware signature mismatch; (2) Secure Boot policy altered; (3) new EFI drivers or hardware devices appear in inventory; (4) system extension loads from unapproved developer IDs post-boot.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0368"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0018","component":"Host Status","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=1166, 7045","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1035","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1035","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0018/"},{"component_id":"DC0059","component":"File Metadata","name":"WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-CodeIntegrity/Operational","channel":"Code integrity violations in boot-start drivers or firmware","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1035","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1035","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"component_id":"DC0079","component":"Driver Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=6","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1035","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1035","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"component_id":"DC0016","component":"Module Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=7","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1035","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1035","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"component_id":"DC0035","component":"Process Access","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=10","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1035","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#AN1035","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"component_id":"DC0018","component":"Host Status","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"firmware_update, kexec_load","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1036","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0368#